    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "WHAT A `theorem _ : False` MEANS HERE, since it reads alarmingly out of context. The module declares the five constraints as hypothesis axioms and derives `False` FROM THEM; that is a refutation of their conjunction, i.e. exactly the proposition in `formal.statement`, and the kernel environment is discarded with them. `formal.language` is `smtlib2` and not `lean4` for this reason: the rendered `theorem infeasible : False` carries no content without its hypothesis axioms, so quoting it as the formal statement would be uninformative at best. SCOPE: this is the largest linear-arithmetic reconstruction this repository has run. Measured: all fourteen call sites of `reconstruct_lra_proof` outside this lane's example live in crates/axeyum-solver/src/reconstruct/tests.rs and pass an assertion slice of length 1 (a negative test), 2, or 3. This is 5 constraints over 4 variables with non-unit integer constants, and it went through `try_general_farkas` unchanged.\n\nAxiom footprint corrected 30 -> 26 on 2026-08-15 (coordinator), measured rather than transcribed. The four dropped entries -- False, Eq, Eq.refl, Eq.rec -- are no longer asserted: the rendered module declares False and Eq as `inductive`, with Eq.refl its constructor and Eq.rec its recursor, and Not as a `def`. The module still references all four (False 3x, Eq 7x), so this is a real shrink of the trusted surface, not their removal. It went unnoticed because the checker exited 0 whatever the count was; it now carries `--expect-axioms 26` and fails on drift in either direction, including when the kernel route is never reached.\n\nProse-vs-footprint drift, found again 2026-08-18 (lane `agent-ledger-freshness`) and this time gated. The 30 -> 26 correction above changed `axiom_footprint` and the `--expect-axioms` flag but NOT the two English sentences next to them, so this evidence entry still said `the 30 axioms` and `21 ordered-field prelude` for three days. Re-measuring found a second, larger staleness in the same entry that no number check would have caught: the CONTRAST paragraph described a facade that emits a 21-line structural shim, and the facade has emitted a real 62-line `Lra` module since the dispatch fix of 2026-08-15. `scripts/check-fact-derived-numbers.py` now re-derives every count a fact asserts about its OWN `axiom_footprint` and fails on disagreement; it cannot see the prose claim, which is why that one survived three re-reads.",
